# Carnivorous Cultivator enters prepared (CR 722.3a): a copy of Enroot waits in exile. On turn 5 Bot1 casts that copy (CR 722.3c) for {G}: the Cultivator stops being
# prepared and the copy is gone (CR 722.3d; a copy of a spell is no card, so it leaves nothing in the graveyard, CR 707.10a), and the search takes the Mountain from the library to the graveyard (CR 701.23; the three cards left in the
# library are only counted). The Cultivator attacks the empty board, deals 2 combat damage to Bot2 and its trigger returns the Mountain,
# the only land card in the graveyard, to Bot1's hand.

[Bot1 Deck]
Carnivorous Cultivator
Forest x6
Lightning Bolt
Counterspell
Duress
Mountain
Island
Ornithopter

[Bot2 Deck]
Mountain x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest#2.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Carnivorous Cultivator.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main2]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Carnivorous Cultivator.Prepared = true
? Exile = Enroot
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Exile.Enroot.Cast
! Bot1.Search(Duress)
Bot1.Search(Mountain)
? Bot1.Battlefield.Carnivorous Cultivator.Prepared = (absent)
? Exile.Count = 0
? Bot1.Graveyard = Mountain
Bot1.Attack(Carnivorous Cultivator > Bot2)
[T5 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 18
Bot1.Hand = Forest; Forest; Forest; Lightning Bolt; Counterspell; Mountain
Bot1.Graveyard.Count = 0
Bot1.Library.Count = 3
Exile.Count = 0
Stack.Count = 0
